            {
                "box": {
                    "id": "obj-3",
                    "linecount": 42,
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 30.0, 553.0, 460.0, 626.0 ],
                    "text": "ADClip9 — Airwindows (Chris Johnson)\nPage: https://www.airwindows.com/adclip9/\n\nWhat it is: modernized Airwindows soft-clip clipper. Adds smooth DC coupling\nand a chosen way to relate the clip ceiling to the processed signal. In this\nRNBO port all controls use the original normalized 0..1 values, exactly like\nthe source VST parameters.\n\nParameters (p_boost lastSample... declared order):\n\n- p_boost  (Boost)     0..1, default 0.0\n  Input gain into the clipper. Linearized approximately by ear: internally\n  maps to a 0 to +18 dB range (pow(10, p*18/20)). Useful to push audio into\n  the clipper; 0.5 ≈ +9 dB.\n\n- p_match  (Match)     0..1, default 0.0\n  Same 0 to +18 dB mapping. In mode \"Match\" the plugin applies this gain,\n  clips, then removes the same amount of level so the result is loud but\n  stays level-matched to the input for A/B purposes.\n\n- p_noise  (Noise)     0..1, default 0.7\n  Mix of randomized dither used when reconstructing clipped tops. Built with\n  a squared curve: noiseLevel = 1 - (1-p)^2, so the perceived change ramps up\n  quickly at first. At 0 the clip is fully deterministic; toward 1 the tops\n  are effectively dithered, which lets some \"over\" detail survive clipping.\n\n- p_ceiling (Ceiling)  0..1, default 0.75\n  Absolute clip target applied to the processed signal, same squared taper\n  1 - (1-p)^2 so high settings change little while low settings pull down\n  dramatically. Also scales the slew-limiting post-clip behavior. Practical\n  musical effect: lower values = more aggressive, duller clipping.\n\n- p_mode   (Mode)      0..1, default 0.0 (3 discrete positions, thirds)\n  0.0-0.33  Boost  - just the boosted clipped signal\n  0.33-0.67 Match  - boosted clip, level-matched back down (does not use the\n                     Boost gain for the audible path)\n  0.67-1.0  ClipOnly - outputs the clipped signal minus the dry input scaled\n                     by the gain (the \"difference\" clip, for parallel or\n                     novelty setups)\n\nMusical notes: designed for master/2-buss loudness. Start with mode = Boost,\nraise Boost until the mix gets flatter, then use Noise/Ceiling to taste.\n",
                    "varname": "paraminfo_comment"
                }
            }
        ],
